              69,
              70,
              77,
              78,
              79,
              80
            ],
            "child_comments": [
              0
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2,
            "type": "markdown",
            "color": "turquoise",
            "position": [
              760,
              115
            ],
            "size": [
              820,
              260
            ],
            "data": {
              "text": "## 2. Read grouping\n\nGroup paired short reads, nanopore and PacBio reads separately. Original mode keeps samples separate; grouped mode merges metadata-defined groups; hybrid mode combines grouped and original reads. Empty sample-matched files stand in for missing long reads."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": 3,
            "type": "frame",
            "color": "turquoise",
            "position": [
              730,
              80
            ],
            "size": [
              880,
              3300
            ],
            "data": {
              "title": "Read grouping"
            },
            "child_steps": [
              18,
              23,
              25,
              26,
              27,
              28,
              29,
              74,
              75,
              76,
              102,
              103
            ],
            "child_comments": [
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 4,
            "type": "markdown",
            "color": "green",
            "position": [
              1830,
              115
            ],
            "size": [
              380,
              260
            ],
            "data": {
              "text": "## 3. Assembly\n\nMEGAHIT assembles short reads. metaSPAdes can also use supplied long reads. Alternatively, provide custom assemblies. Their identifiers and order must match the selected samples. QUAST checks the selected assemblies."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": 5,
            "type": "frame",
            "color": "green",
            "position": [
              1800,
              80
            ],
            "size": [
              430,
              600
            ],
            "data": {
              "title": "Assembly"
            },
            "child_steps": [
              101
            ],
            "child_comments": [
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 6,
            "type": "markdown",
            "color": "lime",
            "position": [
              2450,
              115
            ],
            "size": [
              380,
              260
            ],
            "data": {
              "text": "## 4. Coverage strategies\n\nSingle coverage maps each selected sample\u2019s reads to its own assembly. Multi coverage maps all original read samples to every selected assembly. Choose Both to run both branches. Enabled binners use the resulting alignments and contig depths."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": 7,
            "type": "frame",
            "color": "lime",
            "position": [
              2420,
              80
            ],
            "size": [
              430,
              1500
            ],
            "data": {
              "title": "Coverage strategies"
            },
            "child_steps": [
              81,
              82,
