          "90": {
            "type": "subworkflow",
            "name": "Multi-coverage binning (all samples)",
            "label": "Multi-coverage binning (all samples)",
            "tool_id": null,
            "tool_state": "{}",
            "subworkflow": {
              "a_galaxy_workflow": "true",
              "annotation": "This workflow performs multi-sample binning of metagenomic assemblies with CONCOCT, MaxBin2, MetaBAT2, SemiBin and optionally COMEBin, using cross-sample read coverage, and refines the bins with DAS Tool and/or Binette",
              "comments": [
                {
                  "id": 0,
                  "type": "markdown",
                  "color": "blue",
                  "position": [
                    100,
                    165
                  ],
                  "size": [
                    8370,
                    260
                  ],
                  "data": {
                    "text": "## Multi-sample binning\n\n**Coverage:** flatten the original read pairs, form an assembly \u00d7 read-sample cross product, then rebuild paired collections and matching references with Apply Rules. These operations reuse the original FASTQ datasets. Bowtie2 maps every sample to every assembly.\n\n**Binning:** summarize all sample alignments per assembly into coverage matrices. Enabled SemiBin, CONCOCT, MetaBAT2, MaxBin2 and COMEBin branches use cross-sample coverage. CONCOCT read length is estimated automatically from both mates.\n\n**Refinement:** prepare contig assignments for DAS Tool and candidate FASTAs for Binette. Return selected refined bins, quality reports and coverage matrices. Disabled branches are handled through optional bridges."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "type": "frame",
                  "color": "blue",
                  "position": [
                    70,
                    130
                  ],
                  "size": [
                    8430,
                    3600
                  ],
                  "data": {
